 "notes": "90% C.L. upper limit on the axion-electron coupling g_ae for ALP dark matter absorbed via the axioelectric effect, Fig. 6(c) of the paper ('XENONnT (This work)', black curve). Extracted from the vector paths of the e-print figure lower_limits.pdf (stroke width 1.5 black paths inside panel c), with log axes calibrated from tick-label positions; extracted masses fell on a clean grid (1-10 keV step 1, 12-38 keV step 2, 46-138 keV step 2) and were snapped to it. The limit exists only in (1,39) and (44,140) keV/c^2 because the unconstrained 83mKr background excludes (39,44) keV; the drawn curve spans 1-38 and 46-138 keV. Masses converted keV -> eV. The paper also sets a solar-axion limit in the g_agamma vs g_ae plane (panel a, not a mass-coupling plane), a neutrino magnetic moment limit, and a dark photon kinetic-mixing limit (panel d); the ALP DM g_ae curve is the axion mass-coupling result. Signal model follows the XENON1T excess paper (arXiv:2006.09721), which assumes local DM density 0.3 GeV/cm^3 (not restated explicitly in this Letter).",
